# Frontend Animation Rules

## Design direction

Premium dark portfolio with smooth, purposeful motion — not flashy overload.

## Required patterns

- Scroll reveal: use `RevealOnScrollDirective` (`appRevealOnScroll`) on sections
- Stagger: CSS `animation-delay` on list children (max 80ms increments)
- Hover: `transition-all duration-300` + subtle `translate-y` or scale (max 1.02)
- Hero: animated gradient mesh background (CSS only, no canvas game in hero)

## Performance

- Prefer CSS transforms/opacity over layout properties (width, top, left)
- Cap simultaneous animations; unobserve after reveal (Intersection Observer)
- No infinite animations except subtle background gradients

## Accessibility

Always include:

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  *, *::before, *::after {
    animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
  }
}
```

Respect reduced motion in directives — skip observer animation, show content immediately.

## Avoid

- Canvas games or cursor hijacking on main hero (optional easter eggs elsewhere only)
- Glitch effects on primary headings (hurts readability)
- Parallax that causes jank on mobile
